71
00:01:30,383 --> 00:01:32,193
Six-wheelers never came back.

72
00:01:32,823 --> 00:01:33,848
Jump to 2005.

73
00:01:33,848 --> 00:01:35,965
Inside the nose of

74
00:01:35,965 --> 00:01:37,519
the Renault sat a

75
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:38,031
weight,

76
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:39,693
mounted on springs.

77
00:01:39,723 --> 00:01:40,829
When the car went

78
00:01:40,829 --> 00:01:41,482
over bumps,

79
00:01:41,482 --> 00:01:42,739
the weight moved the

80
00:01:42,739 --> 00:01:44,428
other way and calmed

81
00:01:44,428 --> 00:01:45,602
the car down.

82
00:01:45,602 --> 00:01:46,708
So the tyres kept

83
00:01:46,708 --> 00:01:47,493
their grip.

84
00:01:47,523 --> 00:01:49,144
In 2006,

85
00:01:49,266 --> 00:01:50,767
the stewards in Germany

86
00:01:50,767 --> 00:01:51,945
said it was legal.

87
00:01:52,493 --> 00:01:54,041
But the FIA appealed

88
00:01:54,041 --> 00:01:55,836
against its own stewards,

89
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,246
and the device was

90
00:01:57,246 --> 00:01:57,693
banned.

91
00:01:57,723 --> 00:01:59,097
Renault had to remove

92
00:01:59,097 --> 00:02:00,206
